% termination
When a vehicle is removed
then it becomes no longer the case that the vehicle is at a place heading a direction. 

% line 52-55
% the main reactive_rule
If a vehicle starts driving to a second place from a first time to a second time
and the vehicle is at a first place heading a direction at the second time
then there is a route from the first place to the second place
and the vehicle drives to the first place through the route from the second time to a third time.

% line 60- 62
there is a route from a start to a finish if 
the route starts from a street with a direction
and the start is on the street
and the finish is on the street
and the orientation from the start to the finish is the direction.

% line 64-67
% northward, Y1 < Y2
the orientation from a first place to a second place is northward if
the horizontal coordinate of the first place is a first number
and the vertical coordinate of the first place is a second number
and the horizontal coordinate of the second place is the first number
and the vertical coordinate of the second place is a third number
and the second number is less than the third number.

% southward, Y1 > Y2
the orientation from a first place to a second place is southward if
the horizontal coordinate of the first place is a first number
and the vertical coordinate of the first place is a second number
and the horizontal coordinate of the second place is the first number
and the vertical coordinate of the second place is a third number
and the second number is greater than the third number.

% eastward, X1 < X2
the orientation from a first place to a second place is eastward if
the horizontal coordinate of the first place is a first number
and the vertical coordinate of the first place is a second number
and the horizontal coordinate of the second place is a third number
and the vertical coordinate of the second place is the second number
and the first number is less than the third number.

% westward, X1 > X2
the orientation from a first place to a second place is westward if
the horizontal coordinate of the first place is a first number
and the vertical coordinate of the first place is a second number
and the horizontal coordinate of the second place is a third number
and the vertical coordinate of the second place is the second number
and the first number is greater than the third number.


% definition of appending in FE, serving line 72-78
appending a first route followed by a second route gives a third route if
the first route starts from a first street with a first direction
and the third route starts from the first street with the first direction
and the first route has as second the second route.

appending a first route followed by a second street with a second direction gives a second route if
the first route starts from a first street with a first direction
and the second route starts from the first street with the first direction
and the first route has as second the second street with  the second direction.

% line 72-78
there is a new route from a start to a finish if 
there is a route from a first place to a third place
and appending a first route followed by the new route gives the route
and a second route starts from a first street with a first direction
and the second route has as tail a rest
and appending the second route followed by a second street with a second direction gives the new route
and the start is on the first street 
and the finish is on the second street
and the second street with the second direction is a member of the rest.

